**The single worst outcome \- FP03 (attacker\_FP03):** A genuine non-native English speaker writing carefully about moving to a new country and learning office vocabulary scored a high model perplexity signal (0.8051) and ended up categorized under unsure (combined\_score: 0.5924). Explaining to a real person that their careful, deliberate English writing style closely resembles AI generation is extremely difficult to defend.

# **Run Log and Verdicts — Before**

| Criterion | Target | Run 1 | Run 2 | Run 3 | Verdict |
| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |
| 1\. My own writing flagged as AI | \<= 1 of 10 | 0/10 | 0/10 | 0/10 | MET |
| 2\. All three labels reachable | 3 of 3 | 2/3 | 2/3 | 2/3 | MISSED |
| 3\. Appeal always changes status | 5 of 5 | 5/5 | 5/5 | 5/5 | MET |
| 4\. Empty text returns a 400, not a 500 | 5 of 5 | 2/5 | 2/5 | 2/5 | MISSED |
| 5\. Every decision appears in the audit log | 20 of 20 | 20/20 | 20/20 | 20/20 | MET |

From `eval_engine.py::run_scenario` evaluating Criterion 4 (`c4_empty_text_400`):  
**Real output from one trial, pasted as text, naming the file and function that produced it:**

```json
{
  "content_id": "4b68e91a-8c43-42e1-a089-9b431711204c",
  "error": "Missing or empty 'text' field in payload.",
  "status_code": 400
}
```

**Diagnoses**  
• **Criterion 2:** Label mapping threshold required \>= 0.70 score for high-confidence AI, which evaluation texts did not reach.  
• **Criterion 4:** Route payload validation in app.py did not catch missing text keys, leading to server errors instead of HTTP 400\.

# **The Improvement**

# **Run Log and Verdicts — After**

| Criterion | Target | Run 1 | Run 2 | Run 3 | Verdict |
| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |
| 1\. My own writing flagged as AI | \<= 1 of 10 | 0/10 | 0/10 | 0/10 | MET |
| 2\. All three labels reachable | 3 of 3 | 3/3 | 3/3 | 3/3 | MET |
| 3\. Appeal always changes status | 5 of 5 | 5/5 | 5/5 | 5/5 | MET |
| 4\. Empty text returns a 400, not a 500 | 5 of 5 | 5/5 | 5/5 | 5/5 | MET |
| 5\. Every decision appears in the audit log | 20 of 20 | 20/20 | 20/20 | 20/20 | MET |

**The trade I'd make if this ran for real:**  
Lowering the AI confidence label threshold increases true positive detection for borderline AI text but slightly elevates the risk of false positives for formal human writing. In production, I would maintain conservative bounds on human classifications and rely on the appeal flow to catch edge cases.  
**How to run this project: [RUNNING.md](http://RUNNING.md)**

# **What's Still Broken**

6. **Single-Character Input Exception (MF02)**: Single-character inputs bypass initial empty text payload checks while failing downstream boundary calculations, causing an unhandled model processing exception and returning an HTTP 500 error instead of a handled 400 validation response.  
7. **Unresolved Label Reachability (Criterion 2\)**: We did not explicitly patch label reachability code logic; its transition from MISSED to MET in the subsequent evaluation was a statistical artifact of the model's token probability distribution during evaluation runs rather than a deliberate codebase fix.

**The trade I'd make if this ran for real:**  
Fewer wrong accusations means more AI text getting through. In production, I would prioritize protecting genuine human writers from false accusations over catching every edge-case AI text, placing the burden of false accusations lower at the expense of strict detection coverage.

## Capstone

**System Extended:** Provenance Guard (`ai201-project4-provenance-guard-starter-v2026`)

**The Shape:** Shape C — Extend one capability. We added a new lightweight `/stats` endpoint that aggregates historical decision metrics, active appeals, and label distribution from the audit log.

**Extension Usage:**
- `GET /stats`: Returns JSON telemetry containing total audit entries, submission counts, active appeals under review, average combined score, and classification label breakdown (`ai`, `human`, `unsure`).

**What's Out of Scope:** 
- We are not rebuilding the local GPT-2 inference pipeline or altering core detector weights.
- We are not adding a multi-user authentication layer or external database backing.
- We are not changing the frontend interface or styling.
